    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0791" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 840.48/224</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Genoa</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Genoa</hi></placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1914-08-13T14:00:00-05:00" notBefore="1914-08-13T00:00:00+01:00"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Received August 13, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Two German liners here in port, <hi rendition="#italic">Moltke</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">König Albert</hi>. If Government will use its good
                    offices with England, possibly I could arrange sailing these ships to carry home
                    stranded destitute Americans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Jones</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
